### The offscreen viewer of macro/vis_tridents_lyso.mac, which executes this file before the run when tvDraw is 1.
### The look of macro/vis_lyso.mac (4000 x 3000 pixels, the same colours), but with the lead roof see-through
### (alpha 0.25), so that the trident vertex in it shows, and the setup cut open in front of the TOF stations: the
### part at y > -21 cm is kept (the bars reach y = -20 cm), so that every bar and the whole tracks show. The cut
### removes volumes only, not trajectories. Only muon tracks are drawn, mu- red and mu+ blue. The offscreen driver
### draws them one pixel wide whatever the line width, so scripts/thicken_tracks.py widens them afterwards; and it
### hides them behind the roof's see-through faces, and the plates and bars hide them below them (for tens of cm,
### seen from 15 deg above), so each view is also drawn with only the lead walls and the steel beams, the picture
### that scripts/thicken_tracks.py takes the tracks from: they show over everything but the walls. The camera
### and the highlighted bars are set for each picture by the files that analysis/trident_views_select.C writes
### (start: the whole setup, as below). Drawing is off during the run; the job macro turns it on for the review.

/vis/open TSG_OFFSCREEN
/vis/tsg/offscreen/set/size 4000 3000
/vis/tsg/offscreen/set/file {tvDir}/raw/scratch_{tvJob}.png
/vis/viewer/set/autoRefresh false
/vis/viewer/set/culling global true
/vis/viewer/set/culling invisible true
/vis/drawVolume
/vis/viewer/set/background white
/vis/viewer/set/upVector 0 0 1
/vis/geometry/set/visibility WorldLogic 0 false
/vis/geometry/set/visibility LYSOPanelLogic 0 false
/vis/geometry/set/visibility LYSOFrameLogic 0 false
/vis/viewer/set/style wireframe
/vis/viewer/set/hiddenEdge true
/vis/viewer/set/globalLineWidthScale 2
/vis/viewer/set/lightsMove object
/vis/geometry/set/colour AbsorberLogic 0 0.353 0.373 0.400 0.25
/vis/geometry/set/colour LeadWallXLogic 0 0.353 0.373 0.400 1
/vis/geometry/set/colour LeadWallYLogic 0 0.353 0.373 0.400 1
/vis/geometry/set/colour FrameworkFeLogic 0 0.710 0.729 0.761 1
/vis/geometry/set/colour SupportBeamLogic 0 0.710 0.729 0.761 1
/vis/geometry/set/colour FrameworkAlLogic 0 0.659 0.800 0.910 1
/vis/geometry/set/colour ScintillatorLogicX 0 0.302 0.690 0.314 1
/vis/geometry/set/colour ScintillatorLogicY 0 0.302 0.690 0.314 1
/vis/geometry/set/colour TargetLogic 0 0.949 0.612 0.071 1
/vis/geometry/set/colour LYSOPixelLogic 0 0.478 0.251 0.631 1

# open in front of the TOF stations, seen from the -y side a little from above (x to the right), as vis_lyso.mac
/vis/viewer/set/cutawayMode intersection
/vis/viewer/addCutawayPlane 0 -21 0 cm 0 1 0
/vis/viewer/set/viewpointThetaPhi 75 -62 deg
/vis/viewer/set/lightsVector 0.35 -0.55 0.75
/vis/viewer/set/targetPoint 0 0 50 cm
/vis/viewer/zoomTo 1.3

/vis/scene/add/trajectories smooth
/vis/modeling/trajectories/create/drawByParticleID
/vis/modeling/trajectories/drawByParticleID-0/setRGBA mu- 0.89 0.10 0.11 1
/vis/modeling/trajectories/drawByParticleID-0/setRGBA mu+ 0.12 0.35 0.95 1
/vis/filtering/trajectories/create/particleFilter
/vis/filtering/trajectories/particleFilter-0/add mu-
/vis/filtering/trajectories/particleFilter-0/add mu+

/vis/disable
